wn on the coast of Latium, at modern Anzio south of Rome.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antofagasta"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antofagasta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antofagasta</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Antofagasta is a port city in northern Chile and capital of the Antofagasta Region, on the edge of the Atacama Desert.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antoine-de-lamothe-cadillac"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoine-de-lamothe-cadillac.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antoine de Lamothe Cadillac</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antoine de Lamothe Cadillac was a French adventurer and colonial officer in North America.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antoine-iii-de-gramont"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoine-iii-de-gramont.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antoine III de Gramont</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antoine III de Gramont was a French noble, sovereign lord of Bidache and Marshal of France from 1641.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antoine-lefebvre-de-la-barre"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoine-lefebvre-de-la-barre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antoine Lefebvre de La Barre</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antoine Lefebvre de La Barre was a French colonial administrator who established a lasting French settlement at Cayenne in French Guiana in 1664.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antoine-of-vaudemont"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoine-of-vaude