e near the Natchez.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anton-bruckner"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anton-bruckner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anton Bruckner</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anton Bruckner was an Austrian composer and organist, born at Ansfelden near Linz, known for his symphonies and sacred music, including Masses, a Te Deum and motets.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anton-denikin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anton Denikin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anton Denikin was a Russian general and a leading commander of the White movement in the Russian Civil War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anton-florian-prince-of-liechtenstein"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anton-florian-prince-of-liechtenstein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anton Florian, Prince of Liechtenstein</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anton Florian was prince of Liechtenstein from 1718 to 1721.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/anton-gunther-count-of-oldenburg"><span class="enc-name">Anton Günther, Count of Oldenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anton Günther was Count of Oldenburg from 1603 until his death in 1667, and from 1647 also of Delmenhorst.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anton-holovaty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anton-holovaty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anton Holovaty</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anton Holovaty was a Cossack