ass="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Prince Antoni Radziwiłł was a Polish-Lithuanian aristocrat, composer and patron of the arts who married Princess Louise of Prussia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antonie-van-leeuwenhoek"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonie-van-leeuwenhoek.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antonie van Leeuwenhoek</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antonie van Leeuwenhoek was a Dutch draper and self-taught scientist of Delft.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antonin-dvorak"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonin-dvorak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antonín Dvořák</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antonín Dvořák was a Czech composer, born in Nelahozeves near Prague, who drew on the rhythms and other features of the folk music of Moravia and Bohemia, following the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antonin-janousek"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonin-janousek.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antonín Janoušek</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antonín Janoušek was a Czech communist who headed the Slovak Soviet Republic, proclaimed at Prešov in June 1919 with the support of the Hungarian Soviet Republic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antonine-wall"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonine-wall.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antonine Wall</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Antonine Wall was a Roman turf rampart built across the Forth–Clyde isthmus of central Scotland from 142 on the orders of Emperor Antoninus Pius.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antoninus-pius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoninus-pius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antoninus Pius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antoninus Pius was Roman emperor from 138 to 161, adopted heir of Hadrian and adoptive father of Marcus Aurelius.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antonio-beccadelli"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonio-beccadelli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antonio Beccadelli</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antonio Beccadelli (1394–1471), called Panormita after his native Palermo, was an Italian humanist and poet.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antonio-canales-rosillo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonio-canales-rosillo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antonio Canales Rosillo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antonio Canales Rosillo was a Mexican lawyer and federalist soldier from Tamaulipas.</span></a></li></ul>
